WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.443 --> 00:00:01.362
- Hello, everyone.

00:00:01.362 --> 00:00:03.751
So welcome to another
episode of Unlocking Lily.

00:00:03.751 --> 00:00:06.106
It's always been my dream to be a speaker,

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:08.158
which led me to quit my day job

00:00:08.158 --> 00:00:11.014
to work and mentor under Evan full time.

00:00:11.014 --> 00:00:15.181
And all of you are coming
along for the ride with me.

00:00:17.507 --> 00:00:19.762
In every episode, I take
on a different challenge

00:00:19.762 --> 00:00:21.978
to really help me grow as a speaker.

00:00:21.978 --> 00:00:25.114
In this video, I'm going
to be starting with my why,

00:00:25.114 --> 00:00:26.793
because I learned from Simon Sinek,

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:29.182
it's important for you to know your why

00:00:29.182 --> 00:00:32.193
before you know your how and what.

00:00:32.193 --> 00:00:33.070
Hey, everyone,

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:36.621
so today I'm going to be
teaching a one word workshop

00:00:36.621 --> 00:00:38.054
at the library.

00:00:38.054 --> 00:00:40.469
I'm going to do something a
little bit different than usual.

00:00:40.469 --> 00:00:42.615
Instead of telling people what I do,

00:00:42.615 --> 00:00:45.176
I'm going to start with my why.

00:00:45.176 --> 00:00:46.218
I'm really excited,

00:00:46.218 --> 00:00:48.429
because it's something I
have never done before.

00:00:48.429 --> 00:00:51.069
I'm going to go in, grab my husband,

00:00:51.069 --> 00:00:52.778
and we're going to be on our way.

00:00:52.778 --> 00:00:54.747
I'm going to take you all there, too.

00:00:54.747 --> 00:00:57.255
(upbeat music)

00:00:57.255 --> 00:00:58.181
Hello, husband.

00:00:58.181 --> 00:00:59.064
- You!

00:00:59.064 --> 00:00:59.983
- [Lily] Ready to go?

00:00:59.983 --> 00:01:01.245
- Uh, where?

00:01:01.245 --> 00:01:03.828
(upbeat music)

00:01:06.316 --> 00:01:08.114
- We live really far away from Toronto,

00:01:08.114 --> 00:01:11.012
and usually our rides span anywhere from

00:01:11.012 --> 00:01:13.653
an hour to two and a
half hours to three hours

00:01:13.653 --> 00:01:15.202
into the city,

00:01:15.202 --> 00:01:18.510
so the husband and I like to
trade interesting information,

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:21.022
and today he has something
interesting to tell you all.

00:01:21.022 --> 00:01:24.618
- So I did some pretty
intense research on Wikipedia,

00:01:24.618 --> 00:01:26.920
and I checked out the history of Innisfil,

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:29.944
and it comes from the Irish term

00:01:29.944 --> 00:01:33.543
for the mythical name for Ireland,

00:01:33.543 --> 00:01:35.210
which was Inis Fail.

00:01:36.568 --> 00:01:40.011
So yeah, that's probably Gaelic, too.

00:01:40.011 --> 00:01:43.531
- The reason why the husband
did the research on Innisfil

00:01:43.531 --> 00:01:44.906
because we live in Innisfil.

00:01:44.906 --> 00:01:48.468
So to my Irish friends
out there, is that true?

00:01:48.468 --> 00:01:51.524
Does Innisfil translate to Ireland?

00:01:51.524 --> 00:01:52.446
Tell me.

00:01:52.446 --> 00:01:54.170
Leave in the comments below.

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:55.261
I'm curious to find out.

00:01:55.261 --> 00:01:57.844
(upbeat music)

00:01:59.965 --> 00:02:00.843
Hey, everyone.

00:02:00.843 --> 00:02:02.605
So I'm finally here at
the Toronto Library,

00:02:02.605 --> 00:02:04.061
the Malvern division.

00:02:04.061 --> 00:02:06.621
This workshop is extra special for me,

00:02:06.621 --> 00:02:08.633
because I am from Malvern,

00:02:08.633 --> 00:02:11.223
and to be back here feels great.

00:02:11.223 --> 00:02:13.436
It kind of reminds me
of when I was a teenager

00:02:13.436 --> 00:02:15.153
walking up and down these streets,

00:02:15.153 --> 00:02:18.325
and before ... There's some music pumping.

00:02:18.325 --> 00:02:20.456
That's what I remember about Malvern, too.

00:02:20.456 --> 00:02:22.789
Before I go to any workshops

00:02:23.773 --> 00:02:26.045
or any kind of encounter with people,

00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:28.307
I always think about the
intention that I want to set.

00:02:28.307 --> 00:02:32.453
What is the intention that I
want when people are leaving?

00:02:32.453 --> 00:02:34.642
And the intention today is for them

00:02:34.642 --> 00:02:37.115
to feel something that sparks inside them,

00:02:37.115 --> 00:02:39.629
inspire them to go take action

00:02:39.629 --> 00:02:42.858
and go out there and live
an extraordinary life.

00:02:42.858 --> 00:02:44.621
So I'm really excited,
a little bit nervous,

00:02:44.621 --> 00:02:46.016
but mostly excited.

00:02:46.016 --> 00:02:48.453
And we're going to go inside,
and I'll catch you guys soon.

00:02:48.453 --> 00:02:51.036
(bright music)

00:03:01.869 --> 00:03:02.793
So I just had the workshop.

00:03:02.793 --> 00:03:03.890
It was great.

00:03:03.890 --> 00:03:07.535
I couldn't record much
of the people inside.

00:03:07.535 --> 00:03:10.467
It's just a part of library laws.

00:03:10.467 --> 00:03:12.588
But it was good.

00:03:12.588 --> 00:03:13.467
It was really good.

00:03:13.467 --> 00:03:14.770
It was different.

00:03:14.770 --> 00:03:17.618
It wasn't the big group that I'm used to,

00:03:17.618 --> 00:03:19.338
but it became like a one-on-one coaching,

00:03:19.338 --> 00:03:20.941
which is what I love.

00:03:20.941 --> 00:03:22.908
And I think a lot of people
are going to take action,

00:03:22.908 --> 00:03:26.211
and hold themselves accountable,
and do something great.

00:03:26.211 --> 00:03:28.306
A lot of great words came out of it, too,

00:03:28.306 --> 00:03:30.027
which I'm really excited about.

00:03:30.027 --> 00:03:32.837
Anyway, we're going to go and
spend some time with the family.

00:03:32.837 --> 00:03:34.642
See you guys soon.

00:03:34.642 --> 00:03:37.225
(bright music)

00:03:38.089 --> 00:03:42.186
I just got back from doing
the workshop at the library.

00:03:42.186 --> 00:03:44.405
When I was there, I had
so many great memories

00:03:44.405 --> 00:03:45.707
coming back to me.

00:03:45.707 --> 00:03:48.355
I remember when I was a 16-year-old girl

00:03:48.355 --> 00:03:53.170
who had nothing, just big
dreams and a strong work ethic,

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:57.189
and how a lot of people
took a chance on me.

00:03:57.189 --> 00:04:00.492
I had these great teachers,
these great guidance counselors,

00:04:00.492 --> 00:04:03.626
who helped me form a path for myself

00:04:03.626 --> 00:04:05.807
to be able to go out there
and achieve my dreams

00:04:05.807 --> 00:04:08.023
and how they believed in me,

00:04:08.023 --> 00:04:10.405
believed that I was
capable of doing a lot more

00:04:10.405 --> 00:04:13.013
than I was doing at that time.

00:04:13.013 --> 00:04:14.768
And when I was there, I realized that

00:04:14.768 --> 00:04:17.038
I can be that for someone now.

00:04:17.038 --> 00:04:19.054
Number one, I'm not that girl anymore.

00:04:19.054 --> 00:04:21.279
I have a lot to give.

00:04:21.279 --> 00:04:23.375
And number two, I could
do that for someone.

00:04:23.375 --> 00:04:25.182
I can be the guide for someone.

00:04:25.182 --> 00:04:27.656
I could help them pave their path.

00:04:27.656 --> 00:04:29.587
I grew up in a really poor neighborhood

00:04:29.587 --> 00:04:31.398
where a lot of people don't get out.

00:04:31.398 --> 00:04:32.789
I was able to get out.

00:04:32.789 --> 00:04:35.430
I could go back there and
do that for someone else,

00:04:35.430 --> 00:04:39.037
and then hopefully they could
do that for someone else,

00:04:39.037 --> 00:04:42.141
and it all just kind
of comes a full circle.

00:04:42.141 --> 00:04:45.058
And that further solidifies my why.

00:04:46.908 --> 00:04:51.304
My why is to inspire
people to be extraordinary

00:04:51.304 --> 00:04:53.909
so they could inspire
others to do the same,

00:04:53.909 --> 00:04:57.228
and then how we can all
do this together as one.

00:04:57.228 --> 00:04:59.698
That's the reason why I make these videos.

00:04:59.698 --> 00:05:02.038
That's the reason why
I want to go to speak.

00:05:02.038 --> 00:05:04.522
That's the reason why I coach people.

00:05:04.522 --> 00:05:07.042
Everything I do is because of that,

00:05:07.042 --> 00:05:11.209
and being there really,
really confirmed it for me

00:05:12.147 --> 00:05:15.914
even though I was
uncomfortable with it at first.

00:05:15.914 --> 00:05:17.008
I didn't know how to say it.

00:05:17.008 --> 00:05:18.591
But I'm glad I did,

00:05:19.748 --> 00:05:23.346
because it showed me
and proved to me that,

00:05:23.346 --> 00:05:25.179
that really is my why.

00:05:27.911 --> 00:05:29.250
So the question of the day is,

00:05:29.250 --> 00:05:31.001
what is your why?

00:05:31.001 --> 00:05:32.721
Please write in the comments below,

00:05:32.721 --> 00:05:34.657
and I'll join in on the discussion.

00:05:34.657 --> 00:05:36.862
So my last episode, when
I talked about overcoming

00:05:36.862 --> 00:05:40.098
my fear, I said that I wanted to speak

00:05:40.098 --> 00:05:42.828
in front of a lot of people on stage.

00:05:42.828 --> 00:05:44.627
So I think the next thing
I want to do is like

00:05:44.627 --> 00:05:48.794
go on a big stage and speak
in front of a lot of people.

00:05:50.150 --> 00:05:50.983
A lot.

00:05:52.070 --> 00:05:53.708
Hundreds of people.

00:05:53.708 --> 00:05:54.839
That's what I would like to do.

00:05:54.839 --> 00:05:55.978
Yeah.

00:05:55.978 --> 00:05:59.965
So surprise, I actually
have a TEDx Talk coming up

00:05:59.965 --> 00:06:03.564
in Michigan, so for my next challenge,

00:06:03.564 --> 00:06:07.394
I'm going to be bringing
all of you on the road trip.

00:06:07.394 --> 00:06:09.954
I am so excited to bring you guys along

00:06:09.954 --> 00:06:12.005
for my first TEDx talk.

00:06:12.005 --> 00:06:14.195
I have a special shout-out
for Choria Graphic Arts.

00:06:14.195 --> 00:06:16.362
Choria Graphic Arts wrote,

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:37.127
Choria Graphic Arts, first of all,

00:06:37.127 --> 00:06:39.274
thank you so much for
sharing that with us.

00:06:39.274 --> 00:06:42.838
I do want you to know
that you're not alone,

00:06:42.838 --> 00:06:45.137
and it's okay to feel
discouraged from time to time,

00:06:45.137 --> 00:06:48.594
but I want you to know that
we're all rooting for you.

00:06:48.594 --> 00:06:49.982
So thank you so much for watching.

00:06:49.982 --> 00:06:52.108
Every time an episode comes out,

00:06:52.108 --> 00:06:54.291
I get so excited to read your comments.

00:06:54.291 --> 00:06:57.215
And every time you share
something with me in the comments,

00:06:57.215 --> 00:07:00.943
I feel like I know you a little bit better

00:07:00.943 --> 00:07:03.497
and how we're all in this together.

00:07:03.497 --> 00:07:04.964
Again, thank you so much,

00:07:04.964 --> 00:07:08.381
and I will see you guys very, very soon.

